\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Fused retrieval, the cascade's first stage. The cross-encoder is one voter among three rather than the arbiter: dense, lexical, and reranked orderings of the same candidate pool are merged by RRF (Eq.~\ref {eq:rrf}). A passage found by dense retrieval is voted for twice (bi-encoder rank and cross-encoder rank); a passage only the lexical index found is voted for once --- the lexical list is there to rescue passages dense retrieval missed, not to outvote it.}}{14}{figure.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:arch-fused}{{10}{14}{Fused retrieval, the cascade's first stage. The cross-encoder is one voter among three rather than the arbiter: dense, lexical, and reranked orderings of the same candidate pool are merged by RRF (Eq.~\ref {eq:rrf}). A passage found by dense retrieval is voted for twice (bi-encoder rank and cross-encoder rank); a passage only the lexical index found is voted for once --- the lexical list is there to rescue passages dense retrieval missed, not to outvote it}{figure.10}{}}
